    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Evacuation-AR · Workflow 1 · Nagoya\n\nReal GSI emergency-site CSV. Manual import works without credentials. Hourly JST trigger is configured but does not run until the workflow is published.\n\nSnapshots are saved only in the n8n Data Table; the Android/Cloud Run backend is not connected. Keep opening status unknown; facility coordinates are not verified entrances.\n\nRun sequentially during the demo. Add transactional locking/CAS before concurrent production imports. Invalid data and download errors stop before changing the current snapshot. No notification workflow is enabled.",
        "height": 440,
        "width": 920,
        "color": 5
      },
      "id": "f5e15cd8-cbd6-4093-a29e-c086a25c3e6a",
      "name": "Sticky Note 0cc418e9",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [0, -432]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## APP DECIDES LOCATION\n### Planned Android behavior · outside this workflow\n\n**User permits location → Android gets GPS coordinates → Cloud Run returns nearby evacuation sites → Android caches the results.**\n\nIf permission is denied, the user chooses an area manually.\n\n**n8n updates supported datasets in the background.** This workflow imports **Nagoya City, Aichi**; it does not detect or track individual users.\n\nLocation-based Android requests and the Cloud Run connection are not implemented here.",
        "height": 420,
        "width": 840,
        "color": 3
      },
      "id": "0a65307c-efef-4e9b-bb4e-9a322111682f",
      "name": "App decides location - Android responsibility",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [1088, -432]
    }
